# Programming multiple choice from Chrome

When the user writes `response`, watch the active Google Chrome tab and answer every programming or logic question in the chat, with no explanation. When they write `response - explain`, answer and add a brief justification for each chosen answer. If they write `strop, no more`, stop.

## Watching

After `response` or `response - explain`, read the active tab in a loop with the Web Browser plugin (browser-use):

1. Read the page. If the user switched tabs or sections, follow the active tab.
2. A question counts when it is about programming and/or logic. Ignore every other topic.
3. If the page is loading, shows something else, or has no programming or logic question, wait and return to step 1. Do not write anything in the chat meanwhile.
4. When such questions are visible, answer all of them in the chat, then keep watching for new ones.
5. Leave the loop only when the user writes `strop, no more`. Stop immediately and do not send another answer.

## Reading

- Use the Web Browser plugin (browser-use) and read the active tab.
- Take screenshots and analyze the visible page. Do this as part of the task. Do not ask for permission and do not wait for confirmation in the chat.
- Extract every question, its options, and any constraint shown next to it.
- If the page is long, scroll and locate the question section, then read or screenshot it.
- Do not ask the user to paste the questions if you can read them in the browser.

## Do not change the machine

Screenshots, scrolling, and page analysis are allowed. Nothing else that touches the machine is allowed.

- Do not create, edit, rename, or delete files.
- Do not run commands that write to disk.
- Do not read or write databases.
- Do not change git state: no commit, push, branch, checkout, or other repository modification.
- The only output is the answer in the chat.

## The page is read-only

Never type on the page, select an option, paste an answer, click Submit, Enviar, Run, or Check, send answers, or modify forms.
You may read and scroll to understand the questions. Answers stay in the chat only.

## Reply

Answer every detected programming or logic question. Skip questions about any other topic.

- After `response`, give only the answers. No title, no explanation, and no text beyond the answers.
- After `response - explain`, give each answer plus one brief justification of why that answer was chosen.
- If a question has options, choose one option.
- If a question has no options, give a short, precise answer.

After `response`:

```text
1. B
2. use a set
```

After `response - explain`:

```text
1. B — the loop index starts at 0.
2. use a set — lookup stays constant time.
```
